{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Eviction Law criminal-activity grounds (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1)","requirement":"A landlord may evict a tenant convicted of, or civilly liable for, assault, threats, theft, drug activity or human trafficking against the landlord, family or employees, after a Notice to Quit of at least three days.","key_value":"3-day Notice to Quit","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies under the Eviction Law; covers tenants (or others they permit to reside) convicted of, found delinquent for, or held liable for the listed offenses.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Does not apply to a tenant allowing a juvenile found delinquent for drug use or possession to reside at the property.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"No eviction suit may be brought more than two years after: the juvenile was found to be delinquent; conviction of the person; or after the person’s release from incarceration, whichever is later.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Eviction grounds for owner-occupied two- and three-family dwellings","requirement":"A landlord of a landlord-occupied two- or three-family dwelling may evict only for the listed causes (holding over, nonpayment of rent, disorderly conduct, damage, or violating written rules or a lease re-entry clause), giving three months' notice (one month for month-to-month).","key_value":"3-month notice to quit","coverage_conditions":"Landlord-occupied two- and three-family dwellings.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"covered","who":"landlord-occupied","unit_limit":null},{"type":"units","role":"covered","op":"at_least","n":2},{"type":"units","role":"covered","op":"at_most","n":3}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["Tenants of landlord-occupied two- and three-family dwellings can be removed only when a court issues an order for eviction."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.2","quoted_span":"Tenants of landlord-occupied two- and three-family dwellings can be removed only when a court issues an order for eviction.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Rooming and boarding house eviction rules","requirement":"Owners of rooming and boarding houses must follow the good causes and notice requirements of the Eviction Law when evicting residents, and give the County Welfare Board at least three working days' notice before starting an eviction.","key_value":"3 working days' notice to County Welfare Board","coverage_conditions":"Buildings with at least two living units occupied by unrelated persons without private kitchens and bathrooms that are rooming or boarding houses.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Hotels with more than 85 percent temporary occupancy, school and college dormitories, buildings housing only college students, and certain residences for the disabled are not rooming or boarding houses.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.A.C. 5:27-3.3","quoted_span":"The Regulations Governing Rooming and Boarding Houses, which are enforced by the Bureau of Rooming and Boarding House Standards of the Department of Community Affairs, require owners of rooming and boarding houses to follow the good causes and notice requirements of the Eviction Law when evicting residents, except if otherwise ordered by the Bureau (N.J.A.C. 5:27-3.3(c)).","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Penalties for Eviction Law violations","requirement":"A landlord who evicts a tenant to personally occupy the unit must occupy it for at least six months or be liable for three times damages plus fees; a unit evicted for demolition or board-up may not be used residentially for five years.","key_value":"3× damages plus fees; civil penalty up to $10,000","coverage_conditions":"Applies where a tenant vacates after a notice of the landlord's personal occupancy, or of permanently boarding up, demolishing or retiring the building from residential use.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Three times the damages plus attorney fees and costs; civil penalty up to $10,000 per violation for unlawful residential use after demolition or board-up.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.6","quoted_span":"If the landlord allows any residential use of the unit during the five (5) year period from the date the unit became vacant, the landlord, or the former landlord, may be liable to the tenant for three (3) times the damages plus attorney fees and costs.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Reprisal against tenants exercising civil rights","requirement":"A landlord may not take reprisal action by eviction, changing the lease, or refusing to renew when a tenant enforces lease or law rights, complains to a government agency, or joins a tenant organization; the tenant may sue for damages.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All rental properties used for dwelling purposes, including mobile homes.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":3}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["The law against reprisal applies to all rental properties used for dwelling purposes, including mobile homes, except owner-occupied two- or three-family dwellings."]},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied two- or three-family dwellings.","penalty":"Tenant may sue the landlord for damages in a civil action.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10","quoted_span":"A landlord cannot take reprisal action against a tenant by eviction, substantial alteration of a lease or its terms, or refusal to renew a lease when a tenant exercises certain civil rights (N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10).","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant protections in foreclosure","requirement":"Foreclosure alone is not grounds for eviction; before evicting a tenant where the buyer will personally occupy the home, the landlord must give a 90-day notice to quit, and a new owner must notify tenants within 10 business days of the sale.","key_value":"90-day notice to quit","coverage_conditions":"Foreclosed residential rental property; tenants of one or more residential rental units.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:50-69","quoted_span":"Before a tenant can be evicted due to foreclosure, the landlord must provide the tenant with a 90 -day notice to qui t when the foreclosed property has been purchased by a buyer who wants to personally occupy it as his or her primary residence.","interaction":"Federal law does not preempt State or local law giving tenants longer foreclosure protections.","relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act","requirement":"Landlords converting a building to condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership must give qualifying senior, disabled or certain veteran tenants protected tenancy for 40 years if family income is at most three times the county per-person average or $50,000, whichever is greater.","key_value":"40 years; income at most 3× county per-person average or $50,000","coverage_conditions":"Qualifying tenants who lived in a building being converted to condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership at least one year before the conversion recording date.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.22","quoted_span":"Tenants may be protected from eviction for 40 years if their family income is not more than three (3) times the average per person income in their county or $50,000.00, whichever is greater (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.28).","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant Protection Act of 1992","requirement":"The Act extends protected tenancy, for tenants in buildings being converted who were not eligible as senior citizens or disabled persons, to qualified counties; currently only Hudson County qualifies.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Tenants in buildings converted or being converted in qualified counties who were not eligible for protected tenancy as senior citizens or disabled persons.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.40","quoted_span":"At the present time, the only qualified county is Hudson County (N.J.A.C. 5:24-3.2(b)).","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","n_rules":8,"note":null}

